 SELECT Subject, AVG(Marks) AS Average_Marks
 FROM STUDENT_RESULT
 GROUP BY Subject;

Q. Briefly explain the role of OLAP in analysing academic performance data.

ANS:
OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) is used to analyse large amounts of academic data from
different perspectives.
It helps colleges analyse student performance based on subjects, semesters, marks and
departments.

Example:

A college can use OLAP to:
    1. Calculate the average marks of students in each subject.
    2. Compare student performance across different semesters.
    3. Identify students with low marks.
    4. Find the highest-scoring students.
    5. Compare the performance of different departments.

OLAP Operations
 Operation                      Meaning                       Academic Example

 Roll-up                        Summarizes data               Average marks by
                                                              department

 Drill-down                     Shows detailed data           Department-wise to
                                                              student-wise marks

 Slice                          Selects one condition         Results of Semester 5

 Dice                           Selects multiple conditions   DBMS marks of Semester 5
                                                              students


 Pivot                          Changes data view             Compare subjects across
                                                              semesters


SQL Example
 -- Calculate average marks subject-wise
 SELECT Subject, AVG(Marks) AS Average_Marks
 FROM STUDENT_RESULT
 GROUP BY Subject;


Conclusion
OLAP helps colleges understand academic performance, compare results, identify weak
students and make better academic decisions.

